title: Documentation
kind: overview
summary: The entry point of the metafolder documentation.

metafolder keeps metadata about files — and about things that are not files —
as ''metarecords'' in per-directory repositories, served by a daemon and used
through the `mf` command line and a desktop GUI.

!! Topics

* [[Command line]] — `mf`: its options, selectors, field specs and verbs
* [[Configuration]] — one git repository under `~/.config/metafolder/`, merged on update
* [[Data model]] — metarecords, fields and their typed values; reading and editing them
* [[Daemon]] — the server holding your repositories: loading, configuring, its reports
* [[Duplicates]] — finding byte-identical files and deleting the copies you choose
* [[Schema]] — types of metarecords and the constraints on their fields
* [[Security]] — session tokens, sandboxed decoders, no network
* [[Storage]] — the on-disk store behind each repository: checks, backups, how it answers queries
* [[Slow log]] — the operations that took too long, and where their time went
* [[Tasks]] — the daemon's long work, observable and often stoppable
* [[Trash]] — the per-repository bin: trashing, restoring, undoing

!! Catalogs

Every item of these lists exists in the code; the lists are complete.

* [[CLI command]] — every `mf` command
* [[GUI command]] — every command of the GUI's command input
* [[Panel]] — every panel type of the GUI
* [[Shipped script]] — the helper scripts installed with the configuration
